    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0582" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.01/5–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-07T19:00:00-04:00">May 7, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1916. For Murphy. Your 2407, May 5, midnight. The Department approves the
                    proposal of SHAEF to initiate negotiations for Danish Civil Affairs agreement
                    with the Buhl Government. Official confirmation of the composition of the Buhl
                    Government as contained in press reports has not yet been received. Assuming
                    them to be correct, however, you may inform SHAEF that we intend shortly to
                    recognize the Danish Government by means of a request for Davis’<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d566-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">agrément.</hi><anchor n="39" xml:id="d566-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d566-f1" n="38" xml:id="d566-f1-content">
                <p>Monnett Bain Davis, Director of the Foreign Service of the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d566-f2" n="39" xml:id="d566-f2-content">
                <p>As Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
